former mountain retreat used by Nazi dictator Adolf Hitler. Meanwhile, a survey shows most people in Germany feel the days of the governing coalition are numbered. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>France: Hundreds arrested after nationwide protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:490190885b2485618a0dec41908dc7b504af1fde4dd371744d386209114b8ef0</id><updated>2026-10-25T13:16:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-25T12:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/france-protests-more-violence-feared-amid-renewed-demonstrations/live-79748223--43db314a2270.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/france-hundreds-arrested-after-nationwide-protests/live-79748223?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The French government says more than 1,000 people were arrested following nationwide protests on Saturday. Police and elite security forces were out in force across the country as clashes broke out.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Brazil votes in tight runoff between leftist Lula and right-wing Flavio Bolsonaro</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4ae6d04a028d5f8c43de7a0aa06b26393e6257b3ee78c8b0db6959d98358fa59</id><updated>2026-10-25T13:16:09Z</updated><published>2026-10-25T11:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/brazil-votes-in-tight-runoff-between-leftist-lula-and-right-wing-flavio-bolsonaro/a-79753924--f6f7682c4c53.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/brazil-votes-in-tight-runoff-between-leftist-lula-and-right-wing-flavio-bolsonaro/a-79753924?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The high stakes election will decide whether Brazil will move toward the right or retain a leftist government.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India news: Rahul Gandhi urges protest against voter deletions, announces November 1 rally</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:666610d05ba9b2a63da288c95ee10add734b3e42d4548460778307b8c2554bcf</id><updated>2026-10-25T13:16:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-25T10:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-rahul-gandhi-urges-protest-against-voter-deletions-announces-november-1-rally/live-79748098--c4b74d8129c2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-rahul-gandhi-urges-protest-against-voter-deletions-announces-november-1-rally/live-79748098?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">India's opposition leader Rahul Gandhi has accused the ruling BJP of "vote theft" and urged people to join a rally in Delhi on November 1. The call comes amid protests over revision of electoral rolls. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Serbia votes in closely fought election as student-led opposition challenges Aleksandar Vucic's grip on power</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3afb6ce2f244449138b794e7727fc1a2e80bbe9dcd46eb27fc64875ddb03e590</id><updated>2026-10-25T13:16:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-25T10:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/serbia-votes-in-closely-fought-election-as-student-led-opposition-challenges-aleksandar-vucic-s-grip/a-79753482--997b00f803c3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/serbia-votes-in-closely-fought-election-as-student-led-opposition-challenges-aleksandar-vucic-s-grip-on-power/a-79753482?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Nearly two years after a deadly railway station collapse sparked mass anti-corruption protests, Serbians are voting in a closely fought election that could end Aleksandar Vucic's grip on power.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Gadi Eisenkot campaigns on Moroccan roots in challenge to Netanyahu</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:acc6ffc26bec7f67849782fb997042cb64b3635836ec8b4555da121e34d1fa83</id><updated>2026-10-25T13:16:21Z</updated><published>2026-1