as-yemen-s-houthis-up-pressure/a-79735138?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The US is helping Saudi Arabia fight the Houthi group in Yemen with AI-assisted targeting. But AI is not a magic bullet, experts say, and there are technological, political and human rights issues to consider.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Bulgaria holds presidential elections amid divisions over Ukraine war</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ca2f60ff890ac461fd8ead05593a9437fced3c13450fcaf981fa4f4f6cf41a85</id><updated>2026-10-25T13:16:30Z</updated><published>2026-10-25T07:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bulgaria-holds-presidential-elections-amid-divisions-over-ukraine-war/a-79753496--1dfd3e71b9ce.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bulgaria-holds-presidential-elections-amid-divisions-over-ukraine-war/a-79753496?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Bulgarians are voting in presidential elections amid security concerns over attacks on ships in the Black Sea. The vote for the largely ceremonial post is seen as a test of the popularity of Prime Minister Rumen Radev.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Trump announces Audi will build $4 billion factory in US</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2c397d83e328f357d543b7f458b5a4ae9265295a48221147368c466042760623</id><updated>2026-10-25T13:15:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-25T04:44:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/trump-announces-audi-will-build-4-billion-factory-in-us/a-79753479--4f2bdda08cd3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/trump-announces-audi-will-build-4-billion-factory-in-us/a-79753479?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After Donald Trump made the announcement at an election rally in Georgia, the German carmaker confirmed plans for a factory in the US state, but noted car production would only start early next decade.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>New York Archdiocese to pay $800 million to sex abuse survivors</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1b8c342f9df8577109cfd345bb4c685283cb3ec0620bd8cc55caed93e140dae1</id><updated>2026-10-25T13:15:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-25T02:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/new-york-archdiocese-to-pay-800-million-to-sex-abuse-survivors/a-79753347--80193959f91a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/new-york-archdiocese-to-pay-800-million-to-sex-abuse-survivors/a-79753347?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Around 1,300 survivors agreed to the $800 million payout from the Catholic Church, marking one of the largest clergy abuse settlements in the US.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Nigeria: Tinubu launches reelection bid amid economic woes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d81126e748eb2531379da149f1115061550ba450f975be0eb8775acce982469a</id><updated>2026-10-25T13:15:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T23:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nigeria-tinubu-launches-reelection-bid-amid-economic-woes/a-79753063--a627d82d207b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nigeria-tinubu-launches-reelection-bid-amid-economic-woes/a-79753063?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">President Bola Tinubu promised "a better tomorrow" for Nigerians while kicking off his next electoral campaign, while also blaming his rivals for poverty plaguing Africa's most populous nation.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine: Starlink satellite speeds restored to normal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c11d4a5eecebf849f63cfc2e66585c2551d855a391138cb04ebbe072082ae61a</id><updated>2026-10-25T13:15:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T19:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-starlink-satellite-speeds-restored-to-normal/a-79752155--bc405a2647f5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-starlink-satellite-speeds-restored-to-normal/a-79752155?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The announcement comes after Starlink and Starshield restrictions had disrupted military operations in Ukraine and sparked tensions with the US.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>German national facing trial for alleged attempt to join IS</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9305da1c1de2999b747d21ba17c9562b6025499a817b33b08bbe30263c7897f1</id><updated>2026-10-25T13:15:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T15:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-national-facing-trial-for-alleged-attempt-to-join-is/a-79751032--cd661b98dd30.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-national-facing-trial-for-alleged-attempt-to-join-is/a-79751032?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A 21-year-old suspect is being held in pre-trial detention for allegedly trying to join the "Islamic State" terror group.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Turkey's new deal on Mediterranean maritime boundaries with Libya is exacerbating issues with Greece and the EU</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8f0515f6b5b60362bbacc2c0f3130f3b862974323198a89ead5e8dad125b96de</id><updated>2026-10-25T13:15:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T14:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/turkey-s-new-deal-on-mediterranean-maritime-boundaries-with-libya-is-exacerbating-issues-with-greece/a-79745971--8e4f859a6229.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/turkey-s-new-deal-on-mediterranean-maritime-boundaries-with-libya-is-exacerbating-issues-with-greece-and-the-eu/a-79745971?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Turkey and Libya plan to redraw maritime boundaries in the Mediterranean as part of a new economic corridor. This has sparked strong protests from Greece, and has also drawn the European Union into the conflict.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Will Guinea-Bissau remain trapped in political chaos?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4417756e2a1e479351e95c753e5f053a07dfa96c53e89a58734e71075d975817</id><updated>2026-10-25T13:15:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T11:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/will-guinea-bissau-remain-trapped-in-political-chaos/a-79734069--662f4c5402cf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/will-guinea-bissau-remain-trapped-in-political-chaos/a-79734069?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Elections scheduled for December 6 in Guinea-Bissau have been postponed indefinitely. No new date has been set, leaving the country's return to civilian rule uncertain.</summary><category term="NRS-Import" /></entry><entry><title>EU moves to loosen rules on pesticide use as experts sound the alarm</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1a28f16933e84e9d4e761d6c0148882b1d22aaa3344c6a87711d52c4d808ea56</id><updated>2026-10-25T13:15:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T10:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-moves-to-loosen-rules-on-pesticide-use-as-experts-sound-the-alarm/a-79646422--0c5446a2b9ff.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-moves-to-loosen-rules-on-pesticide-use-as-experts-sound-the-alarm/a-79646422?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The European Union wants to relax rules for pesticides, saying it will be easier for farmers to adopt more environmentally friendly options. But health and environmental experts say the risks are far too great.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>North Korean leader Kim Jong Un travels to Chinese border city via newly opened bridge</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8b09639fa6b557d7a5b9b41d3044c66db